WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions transcribed from the demo narration. Proper nouns (Kiipling, Hertz,
Da Enzo) are corrected against the on-screen product copy in the recording.

00:00.680 --> 00:02.840
Here's a typical trip. Everything looks

00:02.840 --> 00:04.760
fine to the agent, but Kiipling is

00:04.760 --> 00:05.920
watching in the background.

00:06.996 --> 00:09.316
Right here, Kiipling just caught a flight

00:09.316 --> 00:11.956
delay and it's not just a flight. Three

00:11.956 --> 00:13.836
reservations downstream are about to

00:13.836 --> 00:16.276
break, so Kiipling drafts a fix for each

00:16.276 --> 00:16.676
one.

00:18.484 --> 00:21.644
First, the rental. One tap approved and

00:21.644 --> 00:24.004
it's done. Hertz is notified and pickup

00:24.004 --> 00:25.284
moves to 12:45.

00:25.946 --> 00:29.146
Next, the hotel. Approved, executed.

00:29.266 --> 00:31.026
Check-in shifts to three and the front

00:31.026 --> 00:31.786
desk knows.

00:32.481 --> 00:34.001
And dinner, approved.

00:34.441 --> 00:36.681
The Da Enzo table moves to 8:30

00:36.801 --> 00:37.441
instantly.

00:38.655 --> 00:41.255
That's it. Three approvals, three fixes.

00:41.495 --> 00:43.295
Each one executed the moment it's

00:43.295 --> 00:45.735
approved. The whole day rebuilds itself

00:45.735 --> 00:46.735
around the new arrival.

00:49.979 --> 00:52.179
No scrambling, no phone calls.

00:52.499 --> 00:54.499
That's the shift from reactive

00:54.499 --> 00:56.379
firefighting to proactive trip

00:56.379 --> 00:58.339
management. That's Kiipling.
